<title>SOUTH AFRICA: CHOICE PLUNGES INTO HALF YR LOSS, NO DIV.</title>
<headline>CHOICE PLUNGES INTO HALF YR LOSS, NO DIV.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1996-11-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Half year ended August 31</p>
<p>			(million rand unless stated)	 </p>
<p>    Shr, attrib (cts)     90.4 loss   vs 93.1 profit</p>
<p>    Attrib income	   11.98 loss  vs 11.08 profit</p>
<p>    Pre-tax		   26.68 loss  vs 6.98 profit</p>
<p>    Tax			 0.02 gain   vs 4.82 charge</p>
<p>    Interest paid	   13.41	 vs 14.89</p>
<p>    Turnover		  335.24	vs 432.20</p>
<p>Full name: Choice Holdings Ltd</p>
<p>NOTE - Directors said poultry prices had begun to recover in</p>
<p>September which would result in a significant improvement in</p>
<p>operating income in the second half.</p>
<p>They said a rights issue to raise 102 million rand was fully</p>
<p>subscribed and would relieve the group of its finance charge</p>
<p>burden.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
</text>
